DAY 11 — ARCHIVING & COMPRESSION
Commands Reference Sheet
Machine: Kali Linux | User: raven
==========================================

--- CREATING ARCHIVES WITH TAR ---
tar -cf archive.tar folder/           # bundle files, NO compression
tar -czf archive.tar.gz folder/       # bundle + gzip compress (most common)
tar -czvf archive.tar.gz folder/      # same, but verbose (shows each file)

--- VIEWING ARCHIVE CONTENTS (without extracting) ---
tar -tf archive.tar                    # list contents of uncompressed archive
tar -tzf archive.tar.gz                # list contents of compressed archive

--- EXTRACTING ARCHIVES ---
tar -xf archive.tar                     # extract uncompressed archive
tar -xzf archive.tar.gz                 # extract compressed archive
tar -xzf archive.tar.gz -C /path/       # extract to a SPECIFIC destination folder

--- GZIP / GUNZIP (single file compression) ---
gzip file.txt                           # compress (REPLACES original with file.txt.gz)
gzip -k file.txt                        # compress but KEEP the original file too
gunzip file.txt.gz                      # decompress back to file.txt
zcat file.txt.gz                        # view compressed file's content without extracting

--- ZIP / UNZIP (cross-platform) ---
zip archive.zip file1.txt file2.txt     # zip specific files
zip -r archive.zip folder/              # zip an entire folder (recursive)
unzip archive.zip                       # extract to current directory
unzip archive.zip -d /path/             # extract to a specific directory
unzip -l archive.zip                    # list contents without extracting

--- QUICK FLAG REFERENCE ---
c = create      x = extract     t = list (test)
z = gzip        f = filename follows      v = verbose

